cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FarField
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Guijia
    website: https://123zgj123.github.io
repository-code: https://github.com/123zgj123/FarField
url: https://github.com/123zgj123/FarField
abstract: >-
  FarField is an experimental local research runtime driven by explicit
  ScientificState. A single controller coordinates literature retrieval,
  trajectory-conditioned hypothesis exploration, registered experiments,
  verification, and synthesis through existing research workers.
  Scientific events preserve evidence provenance and support state replay.
  Models propose claims and scripts; trusted admission checks constrain
  world identity, reproduction, and the scope of conclusions. Generated
  data cannot corroborate a claim about the target world. Research-policy
  changes require separate trusted heldout evaluation. The system does
  not establish autonomous discovery or demonstrated live self-improvement.
keywords:
  - scientific discovery
  - automated research
  - reproducibility
  - hypothesis testing
  - experimental design
  - evidence
  - research protocol
